## 9. Conditions of use

The release decision is valid only while these conditions hold:

1. {{tool_name}} is used only for the intended uses and contexts in {{doc_id_01}}; prohibited uses stay prohibited.
2. Only organisation-owned accounts with SSO are used for QMS-relevant work; personal accounts are not.
3. The effective configuration equals the approved baseline in {{doc_id_06}}; every change follows {{doc_id_08}}.
4. Every change to a protected branch passes the human approval gate and the required checks. The AI tool never approves, merges, signs or closes records.
5. Only models inside the approved envelope (section 10) are used; a new model or model version is used only after MA-01{{#policy_pinned}}, and the pinned model changes only through the confirmatory subset in {{doc_id_08}}{{/policy_pinned}}.
6. Every AI-assisted change declares the tool and the model used (trailer and / or PR template).
7. Users complete training on {{doc_id_wi}} before access; access is removed when training lapses.
8. No secrets, PHI or personal data are given to the tool beyond what the contract covers.
9. The vendor monitoring routine runs as defined, and the periodic review takes place every {{periodic_review_months}} months.

Context-specific conditions:

{{#ctx_pr_review}}
- AI review comments are advisory; they are never a required approval or the only verification.
{{/ctx_pr_review}}
{{#ctx_doc_drafting}}
- Document drafting: sources are cited for every factual claim and a human approves a full preview before any write to a controlled record.
{{/ctx_doc_drafting}}
{{#ctx_agents_qms}}
- QMS agents: write scope stays as validated; any change to an agent's definition or model follows {{doc_id_08}} (T2 / T8a) before use.
{{/ctx_agents_qms}}
